    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289-a2-a1">

                <pb facs="0555" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/>

                <p>We, the undersigned, residents of Belfast, county of Antrim, Ireland, being duly
                    sworn, declare and say that we are acquainted with James McHugh; that he was
                    born in county of Tyrone, Ireland, about or in the year 1838; that he went to
                    the United States of America on Wednesday, the 4th day of December, 1863, and
                    that we know him to be a British subject.</p>
                <closer><signed>HUGH C. CLARKE.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>JAMES KAVANAUGH.</signed></closer>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Subscribed and sworn to before me, the mayor
                        of <placeName>Belfast</placeName>, by H. C. Clarke and James Kavanaugh, who
                        are credible witnesses, on <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-09">this
                            9th day of January, 1864</date>, the figures 1863 and also 1864 being
                        just inserted.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>JOHN LYTLE. <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor of
                    Belfast.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
